|name2 = Gaia the Supreme
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gaia the Supreme''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Gaia is very unique in terms of usage: her damage output against traited enemies is ridiculous, eviscerating all that enter her area of attack, but landing those hits in the first place is a challenge, meaning that she only really works with good support and synergy; slapping her into a random lineup will scarcely yield results that live up to her extraordinarily high potential, arguably one of the most ''situationally'' overpowered units in the game and very capable of surpassing [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]] exclusives.

At a glance, it can be easy to overlook the fact that she is the most cost effective DPS with good support units due to the many conditions that she will usually demand and treat her purely as a nuker whose effectiveness is reliant on compatible stage mechanics. As a result, one can severely underestimate her ability to be a generalist midranger who can tackle mixed traited stages, that multiple single-traited nukers would struggle greatly on or be extremely expensive to use, without losing damage. This is an incredibly valuable niche in the endgame, where there are an abundance of rush stages with multiple traits sent out without much cash buildup.

The difference between using Gaia with and without proper support is like day and night. Good supports to use with her include [[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Chronos the Infinite]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]], [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]], [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], etc. These will enable her to consistently crush all opposition with merciless efficiency that only the strongest single-trait nukers can even compare. Her multi-hit is also timed in such a way that when some enemies get knocked back thanks to her high damage, they have time to walk back into her line of sight between attacks.

Her lack of knockbacks and any real way to defend herself also means that she doesn't get many chances - let enemies slip in her blind spot twice and she'll be at their mercy, so it is best to prepare first and have her paired with strong meatshields, midrangers, and other CC units.

It's possible to utilize her 34k durability to tank/rush [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance]] and [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave]] enemies such as [[Tackey]], [[Berserkory]] and [[Two Can]] for some quick damage. You can also precisely position her so an enemy is in her blind spot as a stepping stone, enabling her to snipe with her 550 reach.

Overall, Gaia is a very powerful but delicate unit, who can demolish any non-metal traited enemy but is at the risk of them doing the same to it.

